## 3. App Store Connect API keys

**Where:** `$KEYS_ROOT/appstoreconnect/<name>/`, one folder per purpose, each holding
`api_key.json` (key_id, issuer_id, key_filepath) and `private_keys/AuthKey_<KEYID>.p8`.
A key gives tools access to the account with no password and no 2FA.

{{KEY_TABLE}}

**From the command line (headless `xcodebuild` sees no Xcode account):**

```bash
K="$KEYS_ROOT/appstoreconnect/<name>/private_keys/AuthKey_<KEYID>.p8"
xcodebuild … -allowProvisioningUpdates \
  -authenticationKeyPath "$K" -authenticationKeyID <KEYID> \
  -authenticationKeyIssuerID <ISSUER_ID>
```

**REST API** (`api.appstoreconnect.apple.com`): an ES256 JWT with `kid` = Key ID,
`iss` = Issuer ID, `aud` = `appstoreconnect-v1`. The API can create bundle IDs and
enable capabilities, but **cannot create an App Group** — that happens through Xcode
(automatic signing) or on the developer website.

