## 7. Known traps

- **The personal ID in the development certificate's name is not a team** (section 1).
- **Headless `xcodebuild` reports `No Accounts`** even when Xcode is signed in, so
  automatic signing from the command line can only use existing profiles — unless the
  API key is passed (section 3).
- **The wildcard profile (`*`) strips capabilities.** If the build log shows
  `Provisioning Profile: "…: *"`, every App Group and other capability was removed from
  the signature silently. Check with `codesign -d --entitlements - <app>`.
- **XcodeGen empties entitlements files** when `project.yml` has no
  `entitlements.properties` — the signature then has no App Group.
- **Capabilities added in Xcode's GUI to an XcodeGen project** are lost or empty the
  tracked entitlements file. Declare them in code (section 6).
- **A build signed with Apple Distribution does not open on the Mac** (error 163). Sign
  an ad-hoc copy for local testing.
